<p>Memorial Highway was widened to five lanes. Heavy traffic on the two-lane road had frequently resulted in rear-end collisions. The $1.2 million project added a center turn lane, lighting, a railroad underpass, and a river levee gate at the western access to Mandan Avenue. It also removed hundreds of elm and box elder trees planted in the mid-1920s by Mandan's Daughters of the American Revolution and American Legion Auxiliary.</p>
